  "title": "Auto-enable captions on YouTube videos",
  "summary": "<p>You can now automatically enable captions on YouTube videos embedded in your feeds. Head to Preferences &gt; Stories and check the new “YouTube Captions” option.</p> When enabled, any YouTube video in any story will automatically show captions when you start playing it (assuming the video has captions available). This is great for watching videos in noisy environments, for accessibility, or for following along in a language you’re learning. This works by adding the cc_load_policy=1 pa...",
